{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011Cg8CMEc1iyfpWnDsqhkce", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "# Create an alert rule in Northwind Relay\n\nCreate an alert rule so that Northwind Relay alerts you when a stream stops delivering messages.\n\n## Before you begin\n\n- You have Northwind Relay version 2.4.0 or later. Alert rules are available from 2.4.0.\n- You have the permission to create alert rules. [UNVERIFIED: the permission or role that grants access to Alert rules]\n- You know which stream the rule watches and the delivery gap at which the rule fires.\n\n## Steps\n\nTo create an alert rule, complete the following steps.\n\n1. Click **Alert rules**. The **Alert rules** page opens.\n2. Click **New alert rule**.\n3. In **Stream**, select the stream the rule watches.\n4. In **Evaluation interval**, enter how often the rule checks the stream, in seconds. The default is 60.\n5. In **Delivery gap**, enter the delivery gap at which the rule fires.\n6. Click **Save rule**. The rule appears on the **Alert rules** page as **Normal**.\n\n## Next steps\n\n- Watch the rule for one evaluation interval and confirm it stays **Normal** while the stream delivers."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 9276, "cache_read_input_tokens": 11213, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 9276}, "output_tokens": 85, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "819c5baa-5614-4e20-ba65-9cf2b3712db4", "uuid": "ad095798-225e-49cb-8e73-581073c9b0c7", "timestamp": "2026-10-17T17:22:53.449Z", "request_id": "req_011Cg8CMEN8hGeVrJnCKszWr"}
